WEBVTT Kind: captions; Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
[...]

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Once upon a time, or maybe it should be
twice upon a time, because this story

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:51.000
begins where most stories end, there was
a bit of excitement up on cloud seven.

00:00:51.001 --> 00:00:56.000
On this particular morning, the head angel
had called a conference to talk about

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:01.000
Jeff and Mary,
and their guardian angel Wilbur was late.

00:01:01.001 --> 00:01:05.000
Where is Wilbur? I've sent every cherub
in the place out to look for him.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.001
Hi, you fellas.
Let's get this show on the road.

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:09.001
It's already on the road.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.000
I'm sorry, Chief. We've got so many new

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.001
clients,
we'll have to open a new branch office.

00:01:13.001 --> 00:01:17.000
These clients are your immediate concern,
if you want to keep your license.

00:01:17.001 --> 00:01:20.000
Oh, yes sir, yes sir, yes sir, Chief.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:26.001
Marriages are made in heaven, but there's
follow-up work, too. Jeff and Mary have

00:01:26.001 --> 00:01:29.001
been married for a year,
and they haven't had a real honeymoon yet.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.000
But everything's under control.
They're starting on their honeymoon today.

00:01:33.001 --> 00:01:37.000
That's what they think, too. But they're
going to find out differently, unless

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.001
you get down there right away
and take care of things.

00:01:40.001 --> 00:01:41.001
Something's come up.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.000
Something is coming up in exactly 30 seconds.
Now get going.

00:01:46.001 --> 00:01:47.001
Yes sir, Chief.

00:01:47.001 --> 00:01:49.000
[...]

00:01:52.001 --> 00:01:57.000
Wilbur! Oh, Wilbur!

00:02:13.001 --> 00:02:14.000
Yes, Chief?

00:02:14.001 --> 00:02:16.000
Wilbur, make yourself invisible.

00:02:17.001 --> 00:02:18.001
Oh, I almost forgot.

00:02:40.001 --> 00:02:45.001
I'm sorry, Chief. I've got to get organized.
Besides, no one can see me up

00:02:45.001 --> 00:02:47.001
here. Yes sir.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:48.001
Right, Chief.

00:03:15.001 --> 00:03:16.001
You got everything?

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.001
Everything. Including you.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.001
Well, let's go then.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:32.000
[...]

00:03:32.001 --> 00:03:33.000
Jeff, this is Gordon.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:37.000
Oh, hello, Gordon. And goodbye, Gordon.
Mary and I are just leaving.

00:03:37.001 --> 00:03:39.001
Now wait a minute. Something's come up.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.001
It can't come up.
When I finished the score for the show,

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:43.000
you said I could take Mary on our honeymoon.

00:03:43.001 --> 00:03:45.000
We waited a year now, and we're going.

00:03:45.001 --> 00:03:48.001
Now, hold on, Jeff. It's Sonia.
Her wishing number.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.000
The words are okay,
but she doesn't care much about the music.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.000
If we don't have a new tune by tomorrow

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.001
morning, she's not going to sign for the show.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.001
Look, Gordon,
rehearsals don't start from the [...]

00:03:56.001 --> 00:04:00.000
[...] to be waiting for four weeks yet,
and we're on our honeymoon.

00:04:00.001 --> 00:04:04.000
Now listen, Jeff. If you don't come up
with that new music, there won't be

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.001
any show, and there won't be any honeymoon.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.001
Now you can write a new melody in 24 hours.
It's no problem at all.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.000
You must have at least a
dozen old tunes lying around.

00:04:13.001 --> 00:04:15.000
The wishing song?

00:04:16.001 --> 00:04:18.000
No problem at all.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.001
No inspiration, darling?

00:04:49.001 --> 00:04:51.001
I couldn't write the farmer in the bill today.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.001
A temperamental ballerina, I like to...

00:04:54.001 --> 00:04:55.000
Take it easy.

00:04:55.001 --> 00:04:58.001
Don't get way past dinner time
and you haven't eaten lunch yet.

00:04:59.001 --> 00:05:00.001
I'm not hungry.

00:05:00.001 --> 00:05:01.001
I'll fix some coffee.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:12.001
Yes?

00:05:13.001 --> 00:05:14.000
Hello Mary?

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.000
Yes, Sonia.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:21.001
You tell Jeffery the dear
boy that I love his words.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:25.000
But I want more wishing in the wishing song.

00:05:25.001 --> 00:05:27.001
You're absolutely right.
He couldn't agree with you more.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:30.001
He's working on it right now.
It's almost finished.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:35.000
Goodbye.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:52.000
I wish I had a castle in the sky.

00:05:54.001 --> 00:06:00.001
A way up high where bluebirds like to fly.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:09.001
A cozy little castle with
a hundred rooms or more.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:10.001
Oh dear.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:12.001
Someday.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:19.000
With stars for windows,
clouds for rugs, a rainbow for a door.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:22.001
I wish...

00:06:22.001 --> 00:06:27.000
I just wish I had a decent kitchen.

00:06:30.001 --> 00:06:37.000
I

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:39.000
wish...

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:42.001
I wish the faucet wouldn't drip all day.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:58.001
I wish that refrigerator door
would close and stay closed.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:17.001
I wish I had a stove whose
pilot light was always lit.

00:07:22.001 --> 00:07:29.000
Furthermore, a kitchen phone at hand
when friends call up to chat a bit.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:38.000
Hello, yes, this is Mary. How are you? Bye.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:40.001
They say your kitchen dazzles every eye.

00:07:41.001 --> 00:07:47.000
A brand new sink, a built-in oven,
a new refrigerator and a phone.

00:07:47.001 --> 00:07:50.000
A kitchen phone, a bright red phone.

00:07:50.001 --> 00:07:53.000
I gotta go. Goodbye, goodbye, goodbye.

00:07:54.001 --> 00:07:55.001
I'll call you later.

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:13.001
I wish my living room were all redone.

00:08:16.001 --> 00:08:19.001
New drapes, new rugs, oh, this is fun.

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:28.001
It's nice to have a telephone to
blend with my new drapes and rugs.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:32.000
A living room that's all our own.

00:09:00.001 --> 00:09:03.001
[...]

00:09:03.001 --> 00:09:06.001
The bedroom should be changed completely, too.

00:09:08.001 --> 00:09:13.001
Perhaps a color scheme of gold and blue.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:20.001
New furniture and lots of
room for all my clothes.

00:09:21.001 --> 00:09:25.001
On second thought, I might try dusty rugs.

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:41.000
A lady likes to have a
chance to change her mind.

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:47.000
I might like a yellow room
with turquoise and white.

00:09:47.001 --> 00:09:52.001
And maybe a telephone that lights up at night.

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:55.000
I wish I may.

00:09:55.001 --> 00:09:59.000
I wish I might.

00:10:11.001 --> 00:10:17.001
Hello? Hello?

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:20.000
They hung up.

00:10:21.001 --> 00:10:23.001
It was probably Gordon
sitting there like a vulture.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:25.001
Call him back.

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:27.001
Maybe I'll have him a day or two,
but not tonight.

00:10:28.001 --> 00:10:30.000
I haven't got one idea left
to rub against tonight.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:34.000
His line's busy.

00:10:34.001 --> 00:10:37.000
Well, try it again. If he and Sonia can't wait,
I don't care what they do.

00:10:39.001 --> 00:10:48.001
Why don't we call him later?

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:50.001
No. No.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:51.001
All right.

00:10:56.000 --> 00:11:09.000
Wait a minute. Do that again.

00:11:15.001 --> 00:11:18.001
Yeah. Yeah.

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:20.001
Why not?

00:11:21.001 --> 00:11:22.000
Yeah.

00:11:23.001 --> 00:11:25.000
Again. Do it again.

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:34.001
It

00:11:34.001 --> 00:11:37.001
works.

00:11:46.001 --> 00:11:47.000
[...]

00:11:47.001 --> 00:11:48.000
Of course.

00:11:52.001 --> 00:11:57.001
Hello. Oh, hello, Gordon.

00:11:58.001 --> 00:12:01.001
I've been trying to get Jeff.
Sonia's here. How's it coming?

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:03.001
Wonderful. You want to hear something?

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:06.000
You bet. I'll turn on the speakerphone.

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:09.000
I want Sonia to hear it.

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:12.000
Fine. Listen to this.

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:39.000
Watch the world go by with silver.

00:12:39.001 --> 00:12:42.001
From the moonlight and go from the sun.

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:46.001
In our home, just our home.

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:50.000
Wishing castle in the sky.

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:16.001
I love it.

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:19.001
Such rhythm, such spirit, such re-party.

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:22.000
That's it, kids.
Bring it in, Jeff, and go on to your honeymoon.

00:13:56.001 --> 00:13:40.001
Come on.

00:13:58.000 --> 00:13:59.001
Chief, this is Wilbur.

00:14:00.001 --> 00:14:02.000
Mission accomplished. I'll be right up.

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:03.000
[...]
